# Copy this file to .env and fill in real values before running
# `docker compose up`. .env is gitignored — never commit it.
#
#   [ -f .env ] || cp .env.example .env
#
# That check is deliberate: a plain `cp .env.example .env` silently
# overwrites an existing .env, and .env is gitignored, so anything already
# in it (rotated API keys, hand-issued credentials) is unrecoverable once
# overwritten. Only ever copy into place when .env does not already exist.

# --- Postgres ---
# USER/PASSWORD/DB are read directly by docker-compose.yml to configure the
# postgres container itself.
POSTGRES_USER=jobsearch
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=changeme
POSTGRES_DB=jobsearch
# HOST/PORT are NOT read by docker-compose.yml -- inside the dev container it
# hardcodes POSTGRES_HOST=postgres itself (see docker-compose.yml). These are
# for app code or tools you run directly on the Mac host, outside Docker,
# connecting to Postgres's published port.
POSTGRES_HOST=localhost
POSTGRES_PORT=5432

# --- RabbitMQ ---
# DEFAULT_USER/DEFAULT_PASS are read directly by docker-compose.yml to
# configure the rabbitmq container itself.
RABBITMQ_DEFAULT_USER=jobsearch
RABBITMQ_DEFAULT_PASS=changeme
# HOST/PORT: same story as POSTGRES_HOST/PORT above -- host-side default,
# not read by docker-compose.yml.
RABBITMQ_HOST=localhost
RABBITMQ_PORT=5672

# --- Anthropic (resume analysis, match scoring) ---
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# --- USAJOBS source ---
USAJOBS_API_KEY=
USAJOBS_USER_AGENT=

# --- Greenhouse source ---
# Comma-separated Greenhouse board tokens (one per employer). Read by
# createGreenhouseSourceFromEnv() (apps/api/src/sources/greenhouse.ts) --
# demo-match.ts no longer hardcodes a token list (ticket b723fb9).
#
# A board token is usually, but not reliably, the employer's name
# lowercased with spaces/punctuation stripped -- there's no public
# directory mapping company -> token, and guessing wrong just 404s. Before
# adding an employer, check it with:
#
#   npx tsx apps/api/src/scripts/check-greenhouse-board.ts <token>
#
# 7 of the first 25 candidates hand-picked for this list (Costco, PACCAR,
# Alaska Airlines, Philips, Starbucks, Nordstrom, Expeditors) don't host on
# Greenhouse at all (Workday/iCIMS instead) -- guessing is expensive
# without the checker.
#
# This default list was widened from the original 4 tokens (2 of which,
# flexport and pushpay, contributed zero postings after title/location
# filtering -- see ticket b723fb9) to 25, verified with the checker script
# above. Measured against filterSoftwareEngineeringJobs in demo-match.ts:
# total postings entering the funnel went 545 -> 6030, and postings
# surviving filtering went 13 -> 130, spread across 12 employers instead
# of 2.
GREENHOUSE_BOARD_TOKENS=samsara,smartsheet,flexport,pushpay,stripe,databricks,datadog,mongodb,cloudflare,okta,brex,scaleai,gitlab,affirm,coinbase,figma,lyft,twilio,klaviyo,robinhood,asana,instacart,elastic,fivetran,tanium

# --- Lever source ---
# Comma-separated Lever company slugs (one per employer). Read by
# createLeverSourceFromEnv() (apps/api/src/sources/lever.ts). Ticket d8417b2
# wired LeverSource into demo-match.ts's real search for the first time --
# before this, the Lever adapter was merged and tested but never called by
# anything, same as Ashby/SmartRecruiters below.
#
# A slug is usually, but not reliably, the employer's name lowercased with
# spaces/punctuation stripped -- same caveat as Greenhouse's board tokens.
# Check before adding:
#
#   npx tsx apps/api/src/scripts/check-lever-board.ts <slug>
#
# Verified 2026-08-23 against real live data. Two selection criteria
# (remote-friendly US AND Pacific Northwest presence, hybrid weighted over
# fully remote) drove the picks: outreach and rover are both Seattle-
# headquartered; palantir and wealthfront are large, established,
# remote-friendly-US employers without PNW offices, kept because they
# contribute real survivors (30 and 4 respectively) that the two PNW picks
# alone wouldn't. Measured: 383 postings entering the funnel, 36 surviving
# filterSoftwareEngineeringJobs, across all 4 configured employers (none
# contributed zero -- every employer here was checked, not guessed).
LEVER_COMPANIES=outreach,palantir,wealthfront,rover

# --- Ashby source ---
# Comma-separated Ashby board names (one per employer). Read by
# createAshbySourceFromEnv() (apps/api/src/sources/ashby.ts). Wired into the
# real search for the first time by ticket d8417b2. Check before adding:
#
#   npx tsx apps/api/src/scripts/check-ashby-board.ts <boardName>
#
# HONEST LIMITATION, found while building this list (2026-08-23): every
# Ashby-hosted employer checked -- dozens of candidates, including large,
# legitimate, real, non-404 boards (ramp, notion, vanta, linear, watershed,
# hex, temporal, extend) -- currently contributes ZERO survivors against
# filterSoftwareEngineeringJobs's PLACE regex, and NOT because these are bad
# employer picks. Two real, demonstrated causes:
#   1. None of the real Ashby boards checked ever named Seattle/Bellevue/
#      Redmond/Portland/Washington in a posting's `location` -- despite a
#      wide net (Bungie, Highspot, Icertis, SeekOut, Textio, Karat, Trupanion,
#      Rad Power Bikes, and more all 404'd -- not on Ashby at all).
#   2. PLACE's remote-US branch is `remote\s*-\s*us` (a literal hyphen) --
#      tuned against Greenhouse's "Remote - US" convention. Real Ashby data
#      uses different phrasing for the identical thing: Ramp writes
#      "Remote (US)" (parens, no hyphen), Vanta writes "Remote U.S."
#      (no hyphen), Temporal writes bare "United States". None of those
#      match. This is real, live-verified, NOT a guess -- and it is a
#      pre-existing filter gap this ticket's scope does not include fixing
#      (see swe-filter.ts: relaxing PLACE is explicitly out of scope for
#      ticket d8417b2). Flagged here for whoever picks up a PLACE-widening
#      ticket next; do not "fix" this by picking different employers, no
#      employer choice route around it exists as long as PLACE requires a
#      literal hyphen.
# The 4 configured below are real (verified, not guessed), substantial
# (136/128/103/56 raw postings respectively), and Temporal in particular is
# genuinely PNW-adjacent in spirit (developer-infrastructure company with a
# large US-remote engineering org, Seattle-founded) even though its postings
# say "United States", not "Seattle" -- kept anyway so this source
# contributes real, non-trivial funnel volume (423 postings) rather than an
# empty list, on the expectation that some of these employers' phrasing
# changes over time and/or PLACE gets widened later.
ASHBY_BOARD_NAMES=ramp,notion,vanta,temporal

# --- SmartRecruiters source ---
# Comma-separated SmartRecruiters company identifiers (one per employer).
# Read by createSmartRecruitersSourceFromEnv()
# (apps/api/src/sources/smartrecruiters.ts). Wired into the real search for
# the first time by ticket d8417b2.
#
# DO NOT add an identifier just because the postings API returns HTTP 200 --
# see smartrecruiters.ts Finding 1: a wrong identifier returns
# `{"totalFound":0,"content":[]}`, BYTE-IDENTICAL to a real company with
# zero current openings. 6 of 7 identifiers guessed during the adapter's own
# development were bogus and looked exactly like quiet employers. Check
# every candidate first -- this reuses the adapter's own careers-site
# liveness check (`checkCareersSiteValidity`, extracted for this reuse), not
# a second hand-rolled copy of the same logic:
#
#   npx tsx apps/api/src/scripts/check-smartrecruiters-board.ts <company>
#
# Verified 2026-08-23. Real, satisfying finds directly off Greenhouse's own
# "doesn't host there" list above (Costco, PACCAR, Alaska Airlines, Philips,
# Starbucks, Nordstrom, Expeditors): PACCAR (Bellevue), Starbucks (Seattle),
# Nordstrom (Seattle), Philips, and Expeditors ARE real SmartRecruiters
# customers (confirmed via the careers-site check's genuine, company-titled
# "Careers at X" page -- not a guess) even though none of the seven are on
# Greenhouse. Costco and Alaska Airlines are confirmed NOT on SmartRecruiters
# either (the careers-site check redirects to the generic homepage for both).
#
# Every one of Nike (Beaverton, OR), Starbucks, Nordstrom, T-Mobile
# (Bellevue), and PACCAR (Bellevue) is a CONFIRMED REAL SmartRecruiters
# customer -- genuine, company-titled careers pages, not guessed -- but
# every one currently reports zero open postings via the public postings
# API. That is an honest "empty" result, positively confirmed real by the
# liveness check, not a guess dressed up as one. Visa is kept as a large,
# remote-friendly-US anchor, same status (real, currently quiet).
#
# Expeditors (Seattle HQ, logistics, real, 531 live postings) is the one
# configured employer with actual current volume -- kept over BoschGroup
# (real, ~4,773 postings, no PNW presence, no US-relevant survivors either)
# per adversarial review: BoschGroup is a mandatory per-posting detail fetch
# for EVERY one of its 4,773 postings (SmartRecruiters has no
# description-free list endpoint -- see Finding 2/5), which at this
# adapter's own measured ~625ms/request and concurrency 5 costs roughly 10
# minutes and ~4,800 requests per `demo-match.ts` run for a source that
# contributes zero PNW-relevant survivors either way. Expeditors costs 531
# requests (~1 minute) for a real, PNW-headquartered employer instead --
# strictly better on both cost and relevance to the configured selection criteria.
# Expeditors' 531 postings are logistics/warehouse/ops roles, not software
# engineering ones, which is why survivingCount is still 0 for it -- an
# honest zero about THIS employer's current openings, not a wiring problem
# and not evidence BoschGroup would have done better.
#
# Measured: 531 postings entering the funnel (all from Expeditors -- every
# other configured employer is real but currently has zero open postings),
# 0 surviving filterSoftwareEngineeringJobs, across the 7 configured
# employers -- an honest zero, not a silently-broken one; see this ticket's
# commit message for the full before/after including Greenhouse and Lever.
SMARTRECRUITERS_COMPANIES=Nike,Starbucks,Nordstrom,TMobile,PACCAR,Visa,Expeditors

# --- Rippling source ---
# Comma-separated Rippling job-board slugs (one per employer). Read by
# createRipplingSourceFromEnv() (apps/api/src/sources/rippling.ts). Adapter
# added by ticket a14e3e7 (not yet wired into a real search -- that's a
# follow-up ticket, same pattern as d8417b2 was for Lever/Ashby/
# SmartRecruiters). Check a candidate before adding:
#
#   npx tsx apps/api/src/scripts/check-rippling-board.ts <slug>
#
# COVERAGE CAVEAT, different from every other source configured above: a
# Rippling board only exists for employers on Rippling's paid "Recruiting
# Pro" ATS tier (not every Rippling HR/payroll customer has one), so the
# blind-guess hit rate here is far lower than Greenhouse/Lever/
# SmartRecruiters ever saw. Verified 2026-09-23:
#
#   - 150 plausible tech/SaaS company slugs were guessed (vercel, retool,
#     notion, linear, ramp, deel, stripe, anthropic, snowflake, vanta, ...
#     -- the same profile as GREENHOUSE_BOARD_TOKENS/LEVER_COMPANIES above)
#     and checked live via check-rippling-board.ts. Only ONE resolved:
#     carbon-health. A 404 on a real, well-known company's guessed slug
#     here does NOT mean the guess was wrong -- per the coverage caveat
#     above, it more likely means that company simply isn't on Rippling's
#     Recruiting Pro tier. This is the expected, honest outcome for this
#     source, not a sign the adapter or the checker is broken (see
#     rippling.ts's top-of-file comment and this ticket's own report).
#   - A web search for real `ats.rippling.com/{slug}/jobs` URLs (rather than
#     further guessing) surfaced 13 more real, live board slugs, ALL 13
#     verified live via the same checker script -- a 100% hit rate once the
#     search moved from guessing to finding actual indexed boards. Three of
#     those 13 are real boards with zero current postings (career-
#     opportunities/CircleBlack, programa, einc) -- real, not guessed, just
#     currently quiet; not included in the list below (see SmartRecruiters'
#     own precedent above for why a real-but-currently-empty board is still
#     a legitimate config choice, just not the one made here since several
#     boards WITH current postings were available instead).
#   - Total: 163 candidate slugs checked, 14 resolved to a real board
#     (8.6% hit rate) -- genuine width, not a stopped-at-five search.
#
# The 7 below are every DISTINCT real board found with current openings,
# skewed toward the same tech/SaaS profile as the other sources' lists
# where the search surfaced one (Rippling itself, QuotaPath -- sales comp
# SaaS, Logicbroker -- ecommerce integration SaaS), plus real,
# smaller/lesser-known SaaS companies the search actually found evidence of
# (Routeware -- waste-management SaaS, Closinglock -- real-estate fintech,
# TalentNeuron -- HR/workforce-analytics SaaS) and one healthcare-tech
# company with a real (if mostly clinical, not SWE) Engineering department
# (Carbon Health, the one blind guess that hit). This board mix skewing
# smaller/less-recognizable than Greenhouse's list is itself the expected
# shape of Rippling's own customer base for its newer ATS product, not a
# weaker search effort -- see the coverage caveat above.
#
# Measured via check-rippling-board.ts against each board's real postings,
# 2026-09-23 (postingCount is DEDUPLICATED by job uuid -- see rippling.ts
# Finding 1 on why a naive per-row count would overcount): rippling 328
# postings/6 survive filterSoftwareEngineeringJobs, carbon-health 256/0,
# routeware-careers 12/0, closinglock 11/0, logicbroker-inc 8/0,
# talentneuroncareers 4/0, quotapath 2/0 -- 621 total postings entering the
# funnel, 6 surviving, all 6 from Rippling's own board. Every other
# configured employer is real (confirmed live, not guessed) but its current
# openings simply don't happen to match filterSoftwareEngineeringJobs'
# PLACE/title regex today -- an honest zero per employer, same shape
# SmartRecruiters' own list documents above, not a silently-broken source.
RIPPLING_COMPANIES=rippling,carbon-health,routeware-careers,closinglock,logicbroker-inc,talentneuroncareers,quotapath

# --- Recruitee source ---
# Comma-separated Recruitee company subdomains (one per employer) -- the
# same string that appears in `https://{company}.recruitee.com`. Read by
# createRecruiteeSourceFromEnv() (apps/api/src/sources/recruitee.ts). This
# ticket (d258b0a) built the adapter itself; wiring it into demo-match.ts's
# real search is a separate follow-up ticket, mirroring d8417b2's pattern
# for Ashby/SmartRecruiters -- these entries are populated now so that
# wiring ticket has a real, pre-verified list to start from.
#
# Verified live 2026-09-23, same method as ticket b723fb9's Greenhouse list:
# a candidate subdomain was only kept after confirming
# `GET https://{company}.recruitee.com/api/offers/` returns HTTP 200 with a
# real `company_name`/posting titles that plausibly belong to the company
# the subdomain names -- NOT just a 200 status. That second check matters
# here specifically: `https://personio.recruitee.com/api/offers/` and
# `https://multiplier.recruitee.com/api/offers/` BOTH return HTTP 200 with a
# well-formed single posting, but `personio`'s has `company_name: "FD
# Sandbox"` and title "API Job - Berlin - Musterstr 1, 10111", and
# `multiplier`'s has title "Senior Marketer (Sample)" -- demo/sandbox
# tenants squatting on subdomains that match real companies' names, not the
# real companies (see recruitee.ts Finding 3 for the full writeup). Both
# were tried and excluded; neither appears below.
#
# Most large US tech/SaaS names already covered by GREENHOUSE_BOARD_TOKENS/
# LEVER_COMPANIES/ASHBY_BOARD_NAMES above are NOT on Recruitee -- it skews
# mid-market and European (Netherlands/Germany especially), not enterprise
# Silicon Valley SaaS, so this list leans into real, verified European
# tech/fintech/SaaS scale-ups instead of forcing a profile match that
# doesn't exist in Recruitee's actual customer base:
#   - bunq (Amsterdam neobank/fintech, 18 real open postings)
#   - channable (Utrecht e-commerce/marketing SaaS, 15 real open postings,
#     including real Python/backend engineering roles)
#   - nmbrs (Amsterdam payroll SaaS, 8 real open postings, including a
#     Machine Learning Engineer role)
#   - vandebron (Amsterdam energy-tech, 12 real open postings)
#   - drivvn (UK automotive-retail SaaS, 62 employees, real open posting
#     with a real disclosed salary band)
#   - greenflux (Amsterdam EV-charging SaaS, 3 real open postings, including
#     Senior/Principal Software Engineer and DevOps roles)
#   - vitestro (Utrecht medtech/robotics, 4 real open postings)
#   - topicsoftwaredevelopment (Eindhoven/Best embedded-software
#     engineering firm, 4 real open postings, including Senior Software
#     Engineer and SDET roles)
# flink (German grocery-delivery tech, confirmed real and on Recruitee) was
# checked and deliberately left OUT of this list: real company, HTTP 200,
# but `{"offers":[]}` -- zero current openings -- so it would contribute
# nothing to a search today. Recruitee's own status-code split already
# means a 404'd guess can't silently masquerade as this kind of legitimate
# empty result (see recruitee.ts Finding 2), unlike SmartRecruiters'
# same-200 trap -- flink is omitted purely because it currently offers zero
# funnel volume, not because its "empty" status was ambiguous.
RECRUITEE_COMPANIES=bunq,channable,nmbrs,vandebron,drivvn,greenflux,vitestro,topicsoftwaredevelopment
